    "prompt": "Create a PRODUCTION 2D SPRITE ANIMATION SHEET for the EXACT supplied Runelord creature. Image 1 is immutable character identity; image 2 is cel shading style only. Preserve its face, limb counts, armor, palette, proportions and asymmetry in EVERY frame. TRUE TRANSPARENT background. EXACTLY 4 COLUMNS x 4 ROWS, 16 equally sized square cells, orderly grid WITHOUT drawn dividers or labels. Aim for 2048x2048 pixels. Each cell uses the SAME camera, pixel scale and ground plane at 85% of cell height. Character fits within middle 80% of each cell, no overlap or cutoff. Facing right, shallow three-quarter side game view. Keep both feet planted in idle and hit, same foot positions; no bouncing whole sprite or sliding. Clear articulated limb poses, flat hard-edged cel shadows, no gradients, no added detail. No scenery, baked shadow, text, numbers or border. Cell content row-major:\nROW 1 = FOUR subtle IDLE breathing poses for a seamless loop: resting, mid inhale, full inhale, mid exhale. Feet identical, gentle chest expansion, small head and secondary appendage follow-through. NOT four identical copies. Keep same body size, anatomical landmarks.\nROW 2 = FOUR ACTION poses: anticipation, release/contact, follow-through, recover to original idle stance. Pose must use shoulders/elbows/spine and creature-specific action. Keep anatomy consistent.\nROW 3 = frame 1 HIT recoil, frame 2 HIT recovery, frame 3 WOUNDED IDLE lowered tired posture A, frame 4 WOUNDED IDLE breathing posture B. No gore. Feet planted, tired posture clearly different from brief hit.\nROW 4 = FOUR DEATH poses: knees buckle/body weakens; sink and fold; collapse onto ground; terminal lifeless prone body resting on same ground baseline. Distinctly articulated collapse, not whole-sprite spinning. Last frame fully in cell, keep silhouette recognizable. No flames or VFX obscuring anatomy.\n\nIMPORTANT: no projectiles or detached VFX; emission handled by game. Keep at least 12% empty gutter around each pose, especially extended limbs. All poses SAME pixels per body length, do not scale collapse poses up.\nSoul Leech: limbless segmented serpent with ivory circular mouth. Low hover. Idle subtle segmented wave and small mouth aperture pulse; root height stable. Action coil neck back, extend circular maw to drain, recoil, recover. Death slackens segment by segment and rests in a collapsed coil on ground.\nUse generous EMPTY gutters, each silhouette at most 65% cell width. No pose crosses another cell.",
